        <p>The three deductions add up to $1,060.57, so $3,659.43 reaches the bank. The federal line is the annual $18,186.80 divided by 26 checks, and the FICA lines are the annual $9,388.08 split the same way. A month with three biweekly checks pays $10,978.29 of take-home instead of the usual $7,318.86, which is the only month the check size changes. If a 401(k) contribution starts, it comes off the federal line only: a 5% contribution of $236.00 a check cuts the federal withholding by $56.64 a check and leaves the Social Security and Medicare lines untouched.</p>
